    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KJDQC6EMCTTQFKDBQX9JCG55",
        "created_at": "2026-02-26T19:38:54.292Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\n\n**What**: The Web UI WebSocket connection continually disconnects and reconnects. The `WebSocketManager` in `packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts` has exponential backoff reconnection (1s, 2s, 4s... max 30s, max 10 attempts), but users report seeing frequent disconnect/reconnect cycles in the console logs. This suggests either the server is closing connections, the keepalive/heartbeat mechanism is missing, or reconnection resets are happening incorrectly.\n\n**Where**:\n- `packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts` — The WebSocketManager class. Key areas:\n  - `connect()` (line 150): creates WebSocket, sets up onopen/onmessage/onerror/onclose handlers\n  - `scheduleReconnect()` (line 371): exponential backoff logic, max 10 attempts\n  - `onclose` handler (line 183): triggers reconnect on any close event, even clean ones\n  - No heartbeat/ping mechanism — if the server expects periodic pings, the connection may time out\n- `packages/web-ui/src/lib/stores/connection.svelte.ts` — Connection store wrapping the manager\n- Server-side WebSocket handler (in the daemon code) — check if it sends pings or has idle timeouts\n\n**How**: Investigation and fix areas:\n1. **Add heartbeat/ping**: Implement a periodic ping from client to server (e.g., every 30s). Many WebSocket servers close idle connections after a timeout (often 60s). The client should send a ping command and expect a pong response.\n2. **Don't reconnect on clean close**: The `onclose` handler (line 183) calls `scheduleReconnect()` unconditionally. If `event.code === 1000` (normal closure) and the client initiated it via `disconnect()`, skip reconnection. Currently `disconnect()` clears the timer, but there's a race if onclose fires after disconnect resets state.\n3. **Check server-side idle timeout**: The daemon's WebSocket server may have an idle timeout that closes connections. Either increase it or implement heartbeat to keep alive.\n4. **C
```
